  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1037 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nHot temperatures are expected to continue through the long term \nforecast. The upper ridging mentioned in the short term discussion \nwill remain stagnant across the southwestern CONUS at least through \nFriday. Heat Advisory high temperatures will be possible, especially \noff the Caprock, both Thursday and Friday. Therefore, can expect \nHeat Advisories in the future. An upper pattern change and frontal \npassage this weekend will bring precipitation chances and slightly \ncooler temperatures, although only by a few degrees. An upper trough \nacross New England will move away as a secondary upper trough begins \nto amplify as it translates across the Midwest later in the week. As \nthis upper trough amplifies, the upper ridging will get pushed \nfarther west, although the eastern edge of the upper ridge will \nremain above the FA. At the same time, the upper trough will swing a \nweak front through the region Friday. This will \"cool\" temperatures \nover the weekend, however highs will remain in the mid 90s to lower \n100s over the weekend. NBM has backed off on precipitation chances \nwith thunderstorm chances for Thursday mostly to the north of the \nCWA. However chances for thunderstorms, mainly on the Caprock, \nremain forecasted for Friday and Saturday. The upper ridging will \npush back east across the forecast area early next week bringing \ntriple digit temperatures and dry conditions again.",
